  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The polyhedron is a **hexagonal pyramid** since it is a pyramid whose base is a hexagon.  \n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular pyramid because it does not have a rectangle as its base.\n\n- The solid is not a triangular pyramid because not all of its faces are triangles.\n\n- The solid is not a hexagonal prism since it has only one hexagonal face.\n\n- The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-69864\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The polyhedron is a <strong>hexagonal pyramid</strong> since it is a pyramid whose base is a hexagon.  </p>\n<p>Also, notice that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The solid is not a rectangular pyramid because it does not have a rectangle as its base. </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a triangular pyramid because not all of its faces are triangles. </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a hexagonal prism since it has only one hexagonal face.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a rectangular prism since not all of its faces are rectangles. </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
